 # Marching Cubes
 
-Also called: Marching Cubes 3D, Marching Cubes: A High Resolution 3D Surface Construction Algorithm, Polygonising a scalar field
+Also called: 3D Model X-Ray, Bourke's Marching Cubes, Isosurface Extraction, Marching Cubes 3D, Marching Cubes IsoSurface Extraction, Marching Cubes: A High Resolution 3D Surface Construction Algorithm, Polygonise, Polygonizing a scalar field, Voxel New Triangle generation
 
 ## Overview
-Marching Cubes is an isosurface extraction algorithm that generates a triangular mesh from a 3D scalar field by processing each voxel (cube) independently [S1, S2, S3, unofficial]. It determines the topology of the isosurface intersection with the cube boundaries based on the scalar values at the cube's vertices relative to an isolevel [S2, unofficial]. Unlike [Dual Contouring](778-dual-contouring.md), which minimizes error to fit complex features, Marching Cubes uses a fixed lookup table to resolve intersections, making it simpler but prone to topological ambiguities in specific configurations [S1, unofficial]. It builds on the general concept of [Isosurface extraction](30-isosurface-extraction.md) by providing a specific, table-driven method for the cubic grid case.
+Marching Cubes is an isosurface extraction algorithm that generates a triangular mesh from a 3D scalar field by processing each voxel (cube) independently [S2, unofficial][S3, unofficial]. It determines the topology of the isosurface intersection with the cube boundaries based on the scalar values at the cube's vertices relative to an isolevel [S2, unofficial]. It builds on the general concept of [Isosurface extraction](30-isosurface-extraction.md) by providing a specific, table-driven method for the cubic grid case [S2, unofficial]. Unlike [Dual Contouring](778-dual-contouring.md), which minimizes error to fit complex features, Marching Cubes uses a fixed lookup table to resolve intersections, making it simpler but prone to topological ambiguities in specific configurations [S1, unofficial].
 
