 **Algorithm Steps:**
-1.  Iterate through every voxel $(x, y, z)$ in the grid bounds [S2, unofficial].
-2.  Evaluate the scalar field $f$ at the 8 vertices of the voxel:
-    $$ f_v = f(x + v_{pos}[0], y + v_{pos}[1], z + v_{pos}[2]) \quad \text{for } v \in 0..7 $$ [S2, unofficial]
-3.  Compute the **cube index** (case) by checking if each vertex value is greater than or equal to the isolevel $I$. Set bit $v$ if $f_v \ge I$:
-    $$ \text{case} = \sum_{v=0}^{7} 2^v \cdot \mathbb{I}(f_v \ge I) $$ [S2, unofficial]
-    *Note: Some sources define the bit set if $f_v < I$ [S1, S2, unofficial]. The implementation must be consistent with the lookup table. The provided code uses $f_v \ge I$ [S2, unofficial].*
-4.  If `case` is 0 or 255 (all vertices on the same side of the isolevel), skip the voxel [S1, S2, unofficial].
-5.  Retrieve the triangle definitions from `cases[case]` [S2, unofficial].
-6.  For each triangle (defined by 3 edge indices $e_0, e_1, e_2$):
-    a. For each edge index $e$, determine the two vertex indices $v_a, v_b$ connected by that edge using the edge convention [S2, unofficial].
-    b. Calculate the intersection point $P$ on the edge using linear interpolation [S2, unofficial]:
-       $$ \mu = \frac{I - f_{v_a}}{f_{v_b} - f_{v_a}} $$
-       $$ P = V_{v_a} + \mu (V_{v_b} - V_{v_a}) $$ [S2, unofficial]
-       *Guard:* If $|f_{v_b} - f_{v_a}| < \epsilon$ (e.g., $10^{-5}$), set $P = V_{v_a}$ to avoid division by zero [S2, unofficial].
-    c. Add the triangle $(P_0, P_1, P_2)$ to the output mesh [S2, unofficial].
